# Author lock

Nathan clicking **Save** / **Save all** / Ctrl+S in Roster, the card editor, the Script editor, or the HTML board stamps `author_lock` on that text. Ledger: `data/author-locks.json`. Flags also live on the card in `data/content-board.json` and on each row in `data/player-copy.json`.

## Every message

Read `data/author-locks.json` (and the flags on the board / script). Treat locked fields as finished writing unless a Save this session overwrote them.

## Do not

- Do not restyle, Title Case, keyword-paint, shorten, or “clean up” locked copy he did not ask to replace.
- Do not strip `author_lock`, `locked_fields`, or `locked_at`.

## Save is the overwrite

If he typed into an official field (Ability, Call name, numbers, Flow, and so on) and clicked Save, that text is the new locked text. Chat may not restyle it.

If he typed into **Your notes for Cursor** and clicked Save, that note is also a real overwrite for the fields it replaces (Ability, Call name, ATK, HP, and so on). Write the new text into those official fields. Delete the old sentences. Keep the lock flags.

Only stop to ask when the note is confusing, or you cannot tell which locked field it replaces.

## If chat asks to change locked text (no gold-box note, no editor Save)

1. Stop. Do not edit it in that turn.
2. Name the locked keys (card id + fields, or script key + current line).
3. Ask whether this message is an override.
4. Change them only after he clearly says yes to those named keys.

`status` (`todo` / `live` / `hold`) is not locked. You may still implement Flow and set `live` after shipping behavior. After a gold-box ship, clear `review_note`.
